# 📊 Employee Performance Analysis Using Python

## 📌 Project Overview
This project focuses on analyzing employee performance using Python. It explores employee attendance, completed projects, performance scores, salaries, and department-wise statistics to identify trends and generate meaningful business insights.

## 🎯 Project Objectives
- Analyze overall employee performance.
- Identify top and lowest-performing employees.
- Compare performance across departments.
- Analyze employee attendance and project completion.
- Explore relationships between performance, attendance, and salary.
- Generate analytical reports and visualizations.

## 🛠️ Tools & Technologies
- Python
- Pandas
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- Jupyter Notebook

## 📂 Dataset Description
The dataset contains 100 employee records with the following information:
- Employee Name
- Department
- Attendance (%)
- Projects Completed
- Performance Score
- Salary
- Month

## 🧹 Data Cleaning & Preparation
- Checked missing values and duplicate records.
- Removed duplicate records.
- Handled missing numerical values using median imputation.
- Converted the Month column into datetime format.
- Checked data types and data consistency.

## 📈 Analysis Performed
1. Overall employee performance analysis.
2. Top 10 employee identification.
3. Department-wise performance comparison.
4. Average attendance by department.
5. Average salary by department.
6. Monthly employee performance analysis.
7. Correlation analysis between numerical variables.

## 🔍 Key Findings
- Total Employees Analyzed: 100
- Average Attendance: 87.03%
- Average Projects Completed: 4.71
- Average Performance Score: 85.46
- Average Salary: 50,640
- Sales department recorded the highest average performance score of 87.585.
- Finance department recorded an average performance score of 84.175.

## 📊 Project Outcomes
- Identified employee performance trends.
- Compared performance across different departments.
- Analyzed attendance and project completion patterns.
- Identified top-performing and low-performing employees.
- Generated summary reports and visualizations.
- Exported cleaned datasets and department-wise reports.

## 💡 Skills Demonstrated
Python | Pandas | NumPy | Data Cleaning | Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) | Data Visualization | Statistical Analysis | Data Interpretation

## 📁 Project Files
- Jupyter Notebook containing the complete analysis.
- Cleaned employee dataset.
